                sections: [
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Your Mind Is an Operating System", body: "Think of your mind as a complex operating system. It runs thousands of processes — habits, emotional reactions, decisions, social behaviors — most of them automatically, without your conscious input.\n\nThe \"Shadow\" is the hidden code. It's the collection of repressed patterns, unacknowledged variables, and automatic subroutines running in the background. You didn't write most of this code. Your family did. Your school did. Your culture did. Your worst experiences did.\n\nThis hidden code causes bugs:\n• Self-sabotage (you're about to succeed and mysteriously blow it up)\n• Relationship patterns (dating the same type, having the same fight)\n• Decision errors (choices that look rational but are driven by fear)\n• Emotional crashes (disproportionate reactions to minor triggers)\n• Performance ceilings (plateaus that coaching and willpower can't break)\n\nShadow integration is the debugging process. Find the hidden code. Understand what it does. Refactor it. Ship the update.\n\nNo faith required. Everything here is grounded in clinical psychology, neuroscience, and observable behavior."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Where the Shadow Comes From", body: "Carl Jung defined the Shadow as the sum of all personality components you've pushed out of conscious awareness because they didn't fit.\n\nIt includes:\n\n\"Negative\" traits you were punished for: Anger (\"don't raise your voice\"), sadness (\"boys don't cry\"), selfishness (\"think of others first\"), sexuality (\"that's inappropriate\"), ambition (\"don't be greedy\").\n\n\"Positive\" traits you were taught were weak: Sensitivity, playfulness, need for rest, creativity, vulnerability, asking for help.\n\nTalents and instincts that were never developed: The artistic kid told to study engineering. The natural leader told to follow the rules. The emotional intelligence that was labeled \"too much.\"\n\nNone of this disappears. It goes underground. And underground code still executes.\n\nThe mechanism is PROJECTION. Your brain automatically attributes your disowned traits to other people.\n\nExample: You suppressed your anger as a child. Now you're hypersensitive to \"angry people\" at work — you see aggression everywhere, even in neutral emails. That's your shadow projecting.\n\nThis isn't moral failure. Neuroscience shows projection activates the same brain regions as threat detection — amygdala fires, prefrontal cortex mismatch. Your brain literally treats your own disowned traits as external threats.\n\nfMRI studies (Ochsner & Gross, 2005) confirm: suppressed emotions increase amygdala activity and reduce rational decision-making. The shadow isn't metaphorical. It's measurable."),
