                subtitle: "Why the same bugs keep recurring",
                emoji: "🔄",
                sections: [
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Karma Is Just a Feedback Loop", body: "Every spiritual tradition talks about \"karma.\" Strip away the mysticism and here's what's left: unconscious patterns create lawful, repeating consequences. Like control theory loops in engineering.\n\nJung noticed this in thousands of clinical cases. People who never examine their shadow experience the same crashes — same relationship dynamics, same career plateaus, same emotional spirals — over and over.\n\nNot because the universe is punishing them. Because unexamined code keeps executing the same output.\n\nHere are the five types of loops:"),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "The Five Types", body: "LOOP 1 — Personal\nYour own repressed choices running on autopilot.\nSymptoms: Self-sabotage, procrastination, burnout, addictive patterns.\nDebug method: Track \"I did it again\" incidents in a log. When does the pattern fire? What's the trigger?\n\nLOOP 2 — Interpersonal\nUnconscious rules you apply to relationships.\nSymptoms: Repeating conflicts, attraction to the same type of partner, pushing away people who get close.\nDebug method: Relationship post-mortem after every significant conflict. What role did I play? What shadow trait am I projecting onto them?\n\nLOOP 3 — Ancestral / Inherited\nBehavioral code passed down through family modeling.\nSymptoms: \"My family always...\" patterns. Alcoholism, emotional shutdown, financial scarcity mindset, conflict avoidance.\nDebug method: Draw a genogram (family tree) of repeating outcomes across 3 generations. The patterns will be obvious.\n\nLOOP 4 — Cultural / Societal\nAbsorbed group norms that suppress parts of you.\nSymptoms: \"Engineers don't cry.\" \"Men don't ask for help.\" \"Success means sacrificing everything.\" \"Showing emotion is weakness.\"\nDebug method: List 5 \"shoulds\" you've never questioned. Where did each one come from? Does it actually serve you?\n\nLOOP 5 — Archetypal\nUniversal human wiring — status, belonging, threat detection.\nSymptoms: Hero/victim loops in your career story. Savior complex in relationships. Constant need for external validation.\nDebug method: Notice recurring story themes in your journal. Are you always the hero? Always the victim? Always the rescuer? That's the loop."),
