                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Your 30-Day Tracker", body: "Run this like any other experiment. Daily entries with these columns:\n\nDATE — When.\nTRIGGER — What happened externally.\nSHADOW PATTERN DETECTED — Which loop fired (personal, interpersonal, ancestral, cultural, archetypal)?\nINTENSITY — 1-10 scale.\nTECHNIQUE USED — Which of the 6 steps did you apply?\nNEW BEHAVIOR TESTED — What did you do differently?\nOUTCOME METRIC — Mood (1-10), productivity (1-10), sleep quality (1-10), relationship friction (1-10).\n\nWeek 1-2: Mostly observation. You're collecting baseline data. Don't try to fix everything — just notice. You might feel WORSE as hidden patterns surface. This is normal. It's called a \"healing crisis\" in psychology or \"debugging overload\" in our framework. The system is exposing bugs faster than you can fix them. That's temporary.\n\nWeek 3-4: Patterns emerge. You'll start seeing the same 2-3 loops firing repeatedly. Now you have targets. Apply Steps 3-6 specifically to these patterns.\n\nEnd of 30 days: Compare your Week 4 metrics to Week 1. Most people report measurable improvement in at least 2 of the 4 outcome metrics."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Risk Management", body: "This is powerful stuff. Handle with care.\n\nWhen to get professional help:\n• Material surfaces that feels overwhelming or is linked to trauma (abuse, violence, loss)\n• You experience prolonged inability to function (can't work, can't sleep, can't eat)\n• Suicidal thoughts arise\n• You feel dissociated (detached from reality, watching yourself from outside)\n\nIn these cases: stop the protocol and consult a licensed psychologist. Jungian analysts and Internal Family Systems (IFS) therapists are specifically trained for this work. This is not weakness — it's the equivalent of calling a senior engineer when you hit a production-critical bug you can't solve alone.\n\nNever use shadow insights as weapons. Understanding someone else's shadow doesn't give you the right to \"diagnose\" them or use their vulnerabilities against them.\n\nDon't skip the boring parts. The daily scan (Step 1) is not glamorous. It's the equivalent of writing unit tests. Nobody loves it. Everybody who does it gets better outcomes.\n\nExpect resistance. The shadow has been protecting you (poorly) for years. When you start exposing it, it fights back. Increased irritability, weird dreams, old memories surfacing, sudden urge to quit the protocol. This is the system resisting the update. Push through Week 2 and it stabilizes."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Why This Matters Beyond Self-Help", body: "Shadow integration isn't just about feeling better. It's about becoming a more effective human.\n\nPeople who complete this process reliably report:\n• Fewer repeating bugs (same problems stop recurring)\n• Better system stability (emotional regulation under pressure)\n• Higher output quality (creativity, leadership, decision-making)\n• Cleaner interfaces with other humans (less projection, less conflict, more genuine connection)\n\nJung spent decades collecting data and testing methods in clinical settings. His student Marie-Louise von Franz documented hundreds of cases. Modern IFS research (Schwartz & Sweezy, 2019) validates \"exiled parts\" as real sub-personalities with measurable autonomic signatures.\n\nThis is not woo-woo. This is root-cause analysis applied to your own mental operating system.\n\nYou don't have to believe anything. Just run the protocol like any other experiment and measure the results.\n\nIf the spiritual language in earlier modules made you uncomfortable — good. This module is proof that every concept in this course has a grounded, evidence-based parallel. The mystics and the scientists are describing the same system. One uses poetry. The other uses data. Same bugs. Same fixes."),
